  "v1_pattern_detail": {
    "method": "Family close verifier V1. Pattern detail: sign changes of the pattern's effect along pixel rows, per 1000 adjacent glass pixels (ripples: Aqua Jelly, normal stage, Wobble 0.6 minus Wobble 0; film: Oil Slick, film stage, default minus Film variation 0; red channel of the float probe). Demo torus at COMP scale 1, 10 and 0.1, camera moved with the scale, 960 x 540. Scratch probe (agents/fix-close-cf/pattern_probe.cjs); the preview test comp_scale_at_object_size_1_gives_k_times_the_patterns uses the same metric.",
    "now": {
      "ripples": {
        "comp_1_object_size_1": 22.4,
        "comp_10_object_size_1": 214.46,
        "comp_10_object_size_10": 22.4,
        "comp_0_1_object_size_1": 4.87,
        "comp_0_1_object_size_0.1": 22.4
      },
      "film": {
        "comp_1_object_size_1": 44.79,
        "comp_10_object_size_1": 274.47,
        "comp_10_object_size_10": 44.79,
        "comp_0_1_object_size_1": 10.35,
        "comp_0_1_object_size_0.1": 44.79
      }
    },
    "c94e849": {
      "ripples": {
        "comp_1_object_size_1": 22.4,
        "comp_10_object_size_1": 22.4,
        "comp_10_object_size_10": 4.87,
        "comp_0_1_object_size_1": 22.4,
        "comp_0_1_object_size_0.1": 214.46
      },
      "film": {
        "comp_1_object_size_1": 44.79,
        "comp_10_object_size_1": 44.79,
        "comp_10_object_size_10": 10.35,
        "comp_0_1_object_size_1": 44.79,
        "comp_0_1_object_size_0.1": 274.49
      }
    },
    "reading": "Now, at Object size 1 a COMP scale of 10 gives 9.6 times the unscaled ripple detail and 6.1 times the film detail (the bands near pixel size count less), a COMP scale of 0.1 about 0.22 times: finer when scaled up, coarser when scaled down. At Object size = COMP scale (what Fit sets) the count equals the unscaled one. On c94e849 it was the other way round: Object size 1 kept the unscaled count, and the fitted Object size gave 1/k as many."
  },
